## **14. Security and reliability**

For a platform capable of interacting with real trading accounts, security cannot be an afterthought.

| Area           | Requirement                                |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Authentication | MFA and secure sessions                    |
| API keys       | Encrypted secret vault                     |
| Permissions    | Role-based access controls                 |
| Trading        | Independent execution authorization        |
| Data           | Encryption in transit and at rest          |
| Audit          | Immutable execution and configuration logs |
| Availability   | Monitoring and recovery procedures         |
| Backups        | Automated backups and restoration tests    |
| Connections    | Authentication, heartbeat and expiry       |
| AI             | Model output validation                    |
| Risk           | Independent trading safety service         |
| Deployment     | Staged releases and rollback               |

The application must clearly distinguish between live, demo, backtest and simulated results. AI forecasts must never be presented as guaranteed returns.

